 "version": 1,
 "about": "Ctrl/Alt/Shift/F-key shortcuts of the familiar office suite and the HST binding (Windows/Linux, Vietnamese UI; platform macos = a macOS-only row, checked with the macOS values). office: the suite's key; key: the HST key code (officecfg Accelerators.xcu); uno: the commands that count as the same action; source: findkey = Word Application.FindKey on the reference PC, tooltip = the suite's tooltip on the reference PC, docs = the suite's published shortcut list; status: match (the key does the suite's action; via = the HST patch that binds it, was = the command it replaced; handler vcl = the window system handles the key, no accelerator may take it), planned (being built in this release), deviation (hst = what HST does, reason; needs the owner's approval). reason says why a row is what it is. Checked by scripts/check-keytips-parity.py.",
 "reference": "HST4, Office 2021 LTSC 16.0.15601 en-US, 2026-11-14 (data/ribbon/office-keytips-reference.json)",
